</ul><h1>Rinse & Repeat</h1><p>The holidays can be stressful because there are so many big things to keep track of.</p>
<ul>
<li>Who’s making what for Thanksgiving?</li>
<li>Who’s staying where?</li>
<li>Who’s cleaning what if you’re hosting?</li>
<li>Who’s bringing what if you’re traveling?</li>
<li>What does everyone want for Christmas?</li>
<li>What topics do you avoid to keep the conversation pleasant?</li>
</ul>
<p>And yet, what often sends things off the rails isn’t failing or forgetting to answer one of these crucial questions. It’s the smaller questions that get overlooked in the scramble.</p>
<p>Take, for example, this seemingly simple question:</p>
<ul>
<li>What’s the coffee situation?</li>
</ul>
<p>Your answer would likely be: “Oh, it’s fine. There’s always coffee.”</p>
<p>But you’re not thinking of coffee for a crowd. Your coffee routine might differ wildly from your guests’ (if you’re hosting) or your host’s (if you’re guesting). You might want a cup when you wake up, and a cup in the mid-afternoon, and that’s it. Or you might drink mug after mug all morning long and cut yourself off at noon.</p>
<p>But not everyone is going to follow your pattern.</p>
<p>This is the trouble with the jumbo coffee pot. Sure, first thing in the morning, it makes sense to have a big carafe of coffee ready, but as some coffee drinkers drop off, it might not make sense to brew a second or a third big pot. Which is to say nothing about preferred strength, taste, et cetera.</p>
<p>And yet, a Keurig is so wasteful.</p>
<p>Unless you have some of these.</p>
<p>They work like standard Keurig pods, except you load them up with whatever coffee you want and then, when the brewing’s done, you just tap the spent grounds out, rinse, and repeat.</p>
<p>(Pro tip, to seem super conscientious if you’re hosting: leave a bucket out for your guests to knock their grounds into. Say, “It’s for my garden.” Then, when they leave, throw the grounds away, because lol, you don’t even have a garden!)</p>
<p>In other words, anyone can enjoy a single cup at any given time without making a bunch of trash. Pretty nice, huh?</p>
